-- SnoozeShare — mock reference data
--
-- Draft for team review. NOT yet run against a real .db file — see PROJECT_STATE.md for status.
-- "Today" for relative dates is 2026-09-22. Covers every enum value in the architecture doc's
-- schema at least once: all BookingStatus values except FORCE_COMPLETED (agent force actions were dropped
-- by W10 decision C22; FORCE_CANCELLED remains for the account-suspension cascade), all 7
-- WalletTransactionType values, all 4 TicketStatus values, both AccountStatus values, both ListingStatus values.
--
-- Confirmed by operator (2026-09-22), now schema/architecture-doc decisions, not assumptions:
--   * No guest-side service fee. bookings.totalAmount = nightlyRateSnapshot * nights. The only
--     platform fee anywhere is the 3% deducted from a host's BOOKING_PAYOUT.
--   * REJECTED and CANCELLED_BY_HOST both trigger a 100% ESCROW_REFUND, same as a guest
--     cancelling >48h out.
--   * (Updated 2026-09-25, W10 decisions C17/C20) Escrow stays held through the 7-day dispute
--     window (checkout + 7d) and while a ticket is open. An agent resolution settles the FULL
--     escrow: guest refund row (TICKET_REMEDY for Accept, AGENT_OVERRIDE for Manual adjustment;
--     no fee) plus a host BOOKING_PAYOUT for the remainder net of 3%. Open tickets therefore sit
--     on CONFIRMED bookings whose stay is over and whose escrow is still held.
--   * currency is "SGD" throughout, not just an example.
--
-- Remaining assumptions (not yet confirmed):
--   * Escrow hold fires at booking creation (F2.1.3), refund fires on cancellation/rejection —
--     this one IS explicit in the backlog/architecture doc for guest cancellation, extended here
--     to rejection/host-cancellation per the confirmation above.
--   * A rejected or guest/host-cancelled booking's availability_blocks row is treated as removed
--     (not included here) — only blocks still in effect today are seeded.

PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF; -- bulk load in one pass; re-enable after if you want to verify

